Best practices for implementing risk assessments in metro projects
Use a consistent methodology. Establish approved risk criteria, templates, review responsibilities and acceptance requirements.

Assess the actual work. Base assessments on site conditions, engineering documents and the planned work method.

Involve the workforce. Supervisors, contractors and workers should contribute relevant practical knowledge.

Connect assessments to permits. High-risk work should not proceed solely because a document has been completed.

Review changes before execution. Changes in design, location, personnel, equipment or work sequence should trigger appropriate reassessment.

Verify controls at the site. Ensure critical precautions are implemented and remain effective.

Track findings to closure. Assign corrective actions, monitor progress and verify completion.

Use AI responsibly. Treat AI-generated insights as supporting information requiring competent human review.
